# Old Netlify address -> the family domain (2026-10-27). A real 301 so search engines move the old address's ranking here.
# Must stay first so it wins over the rules below.
https://nomansskyhub.netlify.app/*  https://nomansskyhub.app/:splat  301!

# 2026-10-04: targets now the real subdomains (atlas./weather./theme./translator./map.nomansskyhub.app).
# Short/memorable paths through nomansskyhub.app, tunnelling to each
# sister project's real Netlify address. Added 2026-08-18 per Tony's ask —
# "easier to type and remember than the long netlify ones." Plain 301
# redirects: Netlify serves these with zero extra setup on a drag-and-drop
# deploy, no signup needed. NOTE: a plain redirect leaves no visit log
# anywhere Tony can see — Netlify's own Analytics is a paid add-on (not
# free/automatic), confirmed via live research 2026-08-18. If real click
# tracking is wanted later, that's a separate follow-up (e.g. a free GA4
# snippet or a Cloudflare Web Analytics tag added to each redirect target,
# or a tiny Netlify Function counter once Hub is GitHub-connected).

/atlas       https://atlas.nomansskyhub.app          301
/weather     https://weather.nomansskyhub.app               301
/theme       https://theme.nomansskyhub.app                 301
/translator  https://translator.nomansskyhub.app    301
/map         https://map.nomansskyhub.app                   301

# Same-origin proxy for the Galactic Atlas API (it sends no CORS header, so the browser
# blocks a direct fetch). 200 = rewrite, not redirect. Same trick as ATLAS. Added 2026-10-02.
/nms-api/*  https://galacticatlas-api.nomanssky.com/api/:splat  200

# Voyager's Haven alliance leaderboard (havenmap.online, by u/IAmThe-Ekimo-1920). No CORS header, so proxied. Added 2026-10-09.
/haven-api/alliances  https://havenmap.online/api/public/alliances?sort=score&limit=50  200
